                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="334-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="334-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="334-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>AKG Acoustics Perception 400</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Perception 400 is a multipattern large-diaphragm FET condenser microphone from AKG&#8217;s low-cost Perception series. It was replaced in AKG&#8217;s product line by the Perception 420, which changed the pad value to -20dB.</p><p>The 400 has a dual-diaphragm capsule that provides three polar patterns, selectable from a switch on the front of the microphone body: Cardioid, Omnidirectional, Figure of 8.</p><blockquote><p><cite>AKG</cite></p><p>The Perception 220, 420, 820, 100, 200 and 400 share the same capsule platform which is is one-inch, center-terminated and true condenser.</p></blockquote><p>Like the rest of the large-diaphragm Perception microphones, the Perception 400 uses an output transformer.</p><p>The mic has a -10dB pad and a high-pass filter; both can be enabled separately via a pair of switches on the rear of the microphone body.</p><p>Perception 400&#8217;s chassis is made of precision-tooled zinc/aluminum alloy and has a stainless steel grille screen that is dent-resistant. It comes complete with a spider-type shock mount in a metal carrying case.</p><p>AKG&#8217;s Perception microphones were designed in Vienna, and are manufactured in China &#8220;under strict quality control&#8221; (according to AKG).<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/AKG-Acoustics/Perception-400">AKG Acoustics Perception 400</a> is also known as: Perception400.</p><p>The mic was released in 2006.</p>
